        <p>- RUMOURED PURCHASE OF BOLD HALL ESIATE. There • listat„ -151 Rend reason to twlipve that the Bold Ball Haat .;.'llear St. Helens, has again changed hands, and B,!mttiv great mining extensions will be made 1:7 the- , 11)0 estate in qiti n is bounded on the north Liaer-,; '-iondon and Norili-Western main line from and tu ma„chester on the west by the St. Helens Raiiwe),.untes line, on the south by the Cheshire Lines sive 8,-; ',4,11d On the east by Buttonwood and en exten- Alain countri lies between the estate and the as it u' the leondiin and North-Western Company tit inteuns between Warrington and Wigan. There is tent erecting hietory attached to the place. The an- 4esaians cobluer Laold was seated On the estate before the uninterr" Peter Bold, M.P"l3' god fortune to retain their pes- ediv ill the male line till 1781. • daughters but Mr. succeeded lier faSine'r rt 7113 died in that year left seven Mr. Peter Patten, of Bark Maria, his eldest daughter. e i:state, and died in 1813. the second (6110141 s , IVarrington, having married and assumad tlEt nan'te eeded ti? the family estates, 'staved upon his (+int- tlrae of Patten. 0 h'.l"d ulna of Bold in addition to is death in 1819; the estates de- married ihs Sereoe 111 h s. daughter Mary, who, in 1823. Illtatriut h...l.lsittllt.",e_leatl: of the Piincess, which took place at X.-etss Prince Eustace Sapiche, . .oghton, tooAltritilteinl rviir'tne Bold estates tell to her siater,the wife of Who by Rwyal license and permission ?att. 160 n Patten, and name of Bold bpinre Hoghton. Another sister .faiins'il.Rdretis, Anna Maria, was married in 1828 to Mr. eldest son of Mr. Thomas Wilson waa NI-Po but. she died in 1846 Mr. Wilson Patten Bator; vird to the peerage in 1874 under the title of the _ 'tuna rleigh of Wiiiinarleigii, Lancaster. lii 1859 4047144t,e5ta, ea were Put up by auction at the Lion cam VI rrington The catalogue comprised 10 lots, (St: 4;1.1114'g 5,798 acres in Bold, Burt onw• oil, and Sutton Itcent --