      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-05-13_WidnesExaminer_art0078" n="art0078">
        <head>UNIVERSAL BOON.</head>
        <p>A UNIVERSAL BOON.</p>
        <p>It is seldom that any discovery of science is such as will benefit ali easses of people. Some of the grea est discoveries a the age, widle proving beneficial to thousands, have 41.0 at least for a time. injured other thousands. liv n some of the best mediclual preparations. howroer much they may do to remove one Onset of tliaease o- suit some ("Institutions. at the same time either deepen the h lal of another disease, or leave it entirely untouched. or, if they benefit one class of patients they may injure another. Now,</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-05-13_WidnesExaminer_art0079" n="art0079">
