        <p>its some sclentiheally compounded preparatioa which will effect ually cope with the prevalent dleeases of this coontrY. which will be certain to do goo 1 when fs,rly triad. which will be equally adapted to the n etis ot the merchant, the profes- . sional man, and he who wins his bread by the sweat of his brow, the clerk. the factory hand, the [Muer, the workers in metals, and the roadside labourers It sh n d also be such a prepssatlon as contains no injurious ingredients. and which may be taken with Impunity by the weak and sickly child or the delicate female, RS we.b as by the stroiagar constituted man. Such a preparatio would indeed be</p>
