        <p>sot any poisonous or other injurious substances, and thou- sands who h we benefitted by its use age, e in saying it is a specific to all symptoms of Indlostion. Nervousness. and Weakness. It is also confidently rem omen uded for Low Spirits Liver Disorders, and Chest Mb-mums The uLparalleled success of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters Us induced unprincipled per-ons to ffer base and spurious imitation.. so-riewhat similar in name and pnearatice, but possessing non • of the virtues rf this great national remedy. Remelts, ei• that mine are genuine mil. as the name Liwilym Bvans is on abel, stamp, and bottle. sold by a I Chemists, in bottles, at is. lid ,2s 9d. and 4.. 61. each. or may be obtained, carriage free, direct from the Proprietors :—Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, L anelly, south Wales.</p>
