        <p>match Walt played on the drpley ground on Saturday in splendid weather. Warrington went in first, and Messrs. Bibby and Bosworth took their places at the wickets to the bowling of Kershaw and Cotton. Una • worth commenced to hit Well and helped the score up tO fourteen when he was bowled by Kershaw. Brown came to the assistaice of 11ib5y, and runs were scored quickly by both batsmen, Brown hitting two boundaries in succession. He was afterwards caught behind the wicket. The remaining players we&amp; soon disposed of, with the exception of Proud, who batted well for his 20 not out, the Warrington , total reaching 72. Cheetha 11/ 13111 ran up a total of 100 winning by 28 runs.</p>
