        <head>GOLF.</head>
        <p>GOLF.</p>
        <p>lathe venti-final round of the Parliament Golf Handi- cap, played on Thursday, Hon. T. W. Leh. M.P.. (receiving ens stroke), beat Mr. Seton-liarr, M.P., by a hole.</p>
        <p>THE DOWAGER DU-CHESS OF SUMER- -. - LAND'S PRISON LIFE.</p>
        <p>The prospects of the release of the Dowager Duchess of Sutherland liefore the expiration of her six weeks' imprisonment, which terminates at the end of the pre- sent month, are now regarded as remote. By order of the Home Secretary, the condition of her Grice has been reported upon hy a medical gentleman deputed for th, purpose, but Mr. Asquith has not yet Peen fit to reduce the sentence. The health of the duchess appears t 4, remain unaltered. Her meals are provided as usual, while she continues to exercise id the grounds of th, female wine stet the ordinary catwicts have returned to thiiir quarters. She continues to receive visits. Iron. her relatives. On Wednesday, by special permitision,shit was visited by Mr. Ludbury, one of her legal advisers, in connection, it is understood, with matter* relating tt. the Sutherland estates.</p>
