        <p>I</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-05-13_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <p>DA RESBIT RY HIGH WAY BOARD.</p>
        <p>A meeting of this Board was held in the court- room, Daresbury, on Thutsday afternoon. Smith Burgess was voted to the chair.</p>
        <p>MISCIALLANEOI7B. The Finance Committee and the Ship Canal Cc,mmitteet. were re-appointed, the only alteration being the aPP°I% meet of Mr. Darlington in place of Mr. joseph Chit plan was submitted from the Manchester Ship Call- Co ,of the proposed new road from Moss-lane to:o4o°re; lane, Moore, in lieu of the ferry me J n existing litCe"B village. Mr. W. Long proposed and Mr. L. °''ee ; seconded "that the plan ot to Ship Canal ColliP0,1; for the abolition of the ferry aid the substitution 0, 3 !road be accepted." The motion was carried. Itewetha ! decided that a rate of 'lid: in the £ be made ! would realize £260 less man the actual expenditure. ALLZOED CLOSING OF A FOOTPATH AT BARNT h°l ON. . The Clerk read the following commuuica he had received from Barnum :—' 13arnrtate a, April 19th, 1893.—At a meeting of the ; payers of the above-named township, a resolution !cell, passed asking the Guardians to inquire if ie opinion Messrs. Brunner, Mond and Co., ha" voZrey authority to close certain roads across the Beatc ,ay Meadows known as Grass-lane End. The right °I .nGI, in question is maintained by some of the old resleeeete who say it was at one time fenced out from the.ver trance, opposite the Red Lion, down to theeeee. rlies Weaver bank, and prior to it going ,into the p'6°73.,, of the said company, there was always a style "hi has been removed. Further particulars will ha eeeted• our representative.—Yours respect! Lilly, Ed ward eeeed. ley, assistant overseer, liarnton."—Mr. BoutledOsclo-se Mr. Brunner, Mond and Co., bought the Iherieeee through which ran the footpath, about two year9ee They had now stopped it by placing a gate at tou',e-tee It was an old road, and was the only place at e'er-0e where they could laud any stuff from the river reee'ree —Mr. Jones said the Ship Canal Co. had stoePe`Jd roads at Moore in a similar maener.—The Clerk IPP ere Highway Board could riot move in 'the mattee."lo Long said the inhabitants !lad a perfect' orade‘i to br